# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary — never line-ending converted.
#
# 2026-09-17: `git add` warned "in the working copy of 'dist/PMN_Latest.pdf',
# LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it". The committed blob
# was verified byte-identical and valid, because `text=auto` detects NUL bytes
# and treats the file as binary. But that is a content heuristic, and a
# corrupted PDF is the one artifact a reader has no way to notice is wrong
# until they try to open it. State the rule instead of relying on the guess.
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
